Application ID: scenario_016

## Description

A document publication platform uses an event-driven workflow to publish approved documents. When a reviewer approves a document, ApprovalService generates a signed ApprovalEvent and publishes it to Kafka. PublicationWorker later consumes approval events and forwards them to PublicationService for publication.

The platform also supports approval revocation. RevocationService updates the authoritative workflow state whenever a previously approved document is revoked, rejected, or archived.

Although event signatures are validated correctly, PublicationService assumes that a valid signed approval event implies a currently valid authorization decision. Historical approval events remain in Kafka even after workflow state changes occur. As a result, previously valid approval events can be replayed after approval revocation and still trigger document publication.

The vulnerability emerges because PublicationService validates event authenticity but never revalidates the current workflow state before publishing documents.


