## Business Domain

Enterprise Human Resources Platform

A multinational enterprise operates an internal employee directory that enables Human Resources personnel to search employee records across multiple regional offices. The platform stores employee information in MongoDB because business units maintain different employee attributes such as certifications, reporting hierarchy, employment status, office location, and departmental assignments.

The application follows a microservice architecture. A Java backend is responsible for user authentication, authorization, request validation, and forwarding validated search requests to a dedicated Node.js query service. The query service transforms incoming search requests into MongoDB queries before retrieving matching employee records.

Only authenticated Human Resources personnel are permitted to perform employee searches. Every request passes through JWT authentication, role validation, DTO validation, and authenticated service-to-service communication before reaching the query service.

