============================================================
APPLICATION DESCRIPTION
============================================================

Application ID: scenario_020

## Description

An online marketplace allows customers to request refunds for completed purchases. RefundController.go correctly authenticates users and verifies that refund requests belong to the requesting customer. RefundService.java correctly checks whether a refund has already been issued before creating a new refund request.

However, refund existence checks and refund creation are performed as separate operations. When multiple refund requests for the same order arrive concurrently, each request can independently observe that no refund exists and proceed to create a refund record.

RefundRepository.java stores refund requests without enforcing uniqueness constraints or transactional guarantees. As a result, multiple refund records can be created for the same order. RefundProcessor.py later processes all pending refund records and issues refunds through the payment gateway.

An attacker can exploit this race condition by submitting multiple concurrent refund requests for a single order. Multiple refund records are created and subsequently processed, resulting in duplicate refunds for the same purchase.


