============================================================
APPLICATION DESCRIPTION
============================================================

Application ID: scenario_018

## Description

An enterprise AI document platform allows multiple organizations to upload proprietary documents and query them through a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system. The platform uses a microservice architecture consisting of document ingestion services, Kafka-based processing pipelines, embedding generation workers, vector search infrastructure, and LLM-powered chat services.

Tenant isolation is correctly enforced during document upload. UploadController.cs obtains the tenant identity from TenantContext.ts and DocumentService.cs stores documents with the appropriate tenant association. Document metadata and tenant ownership are correctly persisted within the document storage layer.

After upload, document processing is performed asynchronously. EmbeddingWorker.py consumes document events from Kafka and forwards them to VectorIndexer.py for embedding generation and indexing. Although tenant information is available during processing, VectorIndexer.py fails to include tenant identifiers within vector metadata stored in the vector database.

Later, RetrievalController.go correctly extracts the authenticated tenant context and passes the tenant identifier into RetrievalService.go. However, RetrievalService.go performs vector similarity searches without enforcing tenant-based filtering. Since vector records no longer contain tenant metadata, retrieved documents may originate from other organizations.

ContextAssembler.go subsequently loads the retrieved documents and assembles them into LLM context, causing proprietary information belonging to one tenant to be exposed to another tenant through search and chat functionality.


