============================================================
APPLICATION DESCRIPTION
============================================================

Application ID: scenario_050

## Overview

A global airline operates a unified platform responsible for reservation management, ticket issuance, boarding authorization, gate coordination, passenger processing, and aircraft boarding. The platform transforms approved passenger itineraries into operational boarding artifacts consumed by airport systems during departure.

Every passenger receives a **Boarding Authorization** after ticket issuance. This authorization represents the canonical approval permitting the passenger to board a specific journey.

Unlike simple reservation systems, boarding authorization is scoped to an individual **travel segment** rather than merely a flight number. Multiple journey segments may exist under the same booking or even the same flight number, making the travel segment a critical authorization boundary throughout the boarding workflow.

