============================================================
APPLICATION DESCRIPTION
============================================================

Application ID: scenario_078

## Description

An enterprise Identity Federation Platform centrally manages certificate trust bundles used by identity gateways deployed across multiple data centers. Instead of allowing gateways to directly communicate with Certificate Authorities, every trust update is first reviewed, approved, packaged, published, synchronized, and finally installed through a controlled distribution pipeline.

Each approved Trust Package is permanently bound to a specific trust lineage identified by:

* Package ID
* Bundle Version
* Trust Generation

The **Trust Generation** uniquely identifies the exact certificate trust hierarchy that was approved during certificate issuance.

Identity Gateways authenticate workloads exclusively using installed Trust Packages and never contact the Certificate Authority during runtime.

---

## Normal Workflow

```text
Certificate Enrollment

        │

        ▼

Certificate Authority

        │

        ▼

Trust Package

        │

        ▼

Package Publication

        │

        ▼

Gateway Synchronization

        │

        ▼

Gateway Installation

        │

        ▼

Identity Gateway

        │

        ▼

Enterprise Authentication

        │

        ▼

Telemetry
```

Certificate enrollment correctly validates workload identity before issuing an approved Trust Package. The Certificate Authority preserves the complete trust lineage throughout approval, while gateway synchronization reliably transports published artifacts between data centers. Identity Gateways correctly activate the installed trust bundle and enterprise authentication proceeds using the supplied Trust Installation Plan.

---


